{"type":"assistant","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"msg_011Cgs2RrgnnpWcZUwHbNXxu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Summary of the session**\n\n- **State:** At turn 196 (spring, year 2) there are 8 settlers, up from 6. Nobody has died. Care penalties look small: one thirst flag, one hunger flag and one tired flag showed up, and each cleared.\n- **Progress:** 1 of 9 Harmony Gate milestones is met (\"Everyone has a bed\"). The next one is 10 people, and I'm 2 short.\n- **Setup:** I saved one `governor` script, now at version 2. It covers research, cabbage harvesting, a stockpile, wood, beds and a plan-driven build list. The plan holds the goal, research order and build queue (Meditation Pavilion, Orchard, Campfire, Farm Plot).\n- **Research:** The queue is empty again, with Windmills the last tech learned. The next step is to add Air Scooter, Cartography and Prospecting to `plan.research`.\n\n**Observations for the designers**\n- Research only progressed once a Meditation Pavilion was built and settlers began \"Study\". Nothing on screen said that was required.\n- Wood came in very fast (107 in about 100 seconds), while the first food income was slow.\n- Most settlers sit idle (\"no reachable job\") once the nearby cabbages and trees are marked, so the game gives little to do after the early work.\n- Population grew by arrivals only (6 to 8 over about two game-years). The game doesn't say what triggers an arrival, so reaching 10 people feels opaque.\n- Bed build sites kept appearing at \"0/5 Wood\". Either my bed count undercounts, or a site waits a long time for hauling.\n- SDK gap: `designate_near` counts \"nothing to harvest\" as a failure, so the run report fills with false failures (21 in one stretch).\n- No SDK call shows whether a Pavilion or Farm Plot actually got built. I could only infer it from the Study activity.\n\nI didn't look at what the Farm Plot and Orchard builds actually did."}]}}
